A '''nonsomatic spell''' is a [[spell]] that lacks a somatic [[component]], so it can be cast while wearing full [[armor]] and [[shield]], ignoring the chance of [[arcane spell failure]] due to armor penalties. This classification is only of interest with regards to [[arcane]] spells; [[divine]] spells receive no special treatment for being nonsomatic.

The nonsomatic arcane spells included in Neverwinter Nights are
''[[blindness/deafness]]'',
''[[darkness (spell)|darkness]]'',
''[[displacement]]'',
''[[flare]]'',
''[[knock]]'',
''[[light]]'',
''[[mass charm]]'',
''[[Mordenkainen's disjunction]]'',
''[[polymorph self]]'',
''[[power word, kill]]'',
''[[power word, stun]]'',
''[[time stop]]'',
''[[true strike]]'', and
''[[wail of the banshee]]''.

In addition, any spell cast with the [[still spell]] (or [[automatic still spell]]) feat is treated as a nonsomatic spell.
Furthermore, [[epic spell]]s are not considered to be arcane by the game engine, so are not subject to arcane spell failure, even if cast by an arcane caster.

